# error: literal_without_token.grammar:24:8:
# error: "go"
#
# A string literal in a rule must name a token: the lexer rule whose
# pattern is exactly that text (or an @op mapping). A literal no lexer rule
# produces is a located generation error naming it.
#
# Today: generation succeeds and the alternative is silently unreachable:
# `go x` lexes as two IDENTs and fails with a ParseError. Found while
# documenting literals.

@lexer
tokens
    ident
    eof
    err
[a-z]+                                      → ident
.                                           → err

@parser
@lang = "literal_without_token"

top! = IDENT                                → (top 1)
     | "go" IDENT                           → (kw 2)
